{
 "copyright": "AI, UI, logging, or other modifications first developed in AdvCiv-SAS (Simple Advanced Strategy). (c) 2026 wonderingabout & AI/LLM helpers (see Authors in AdvCiv-SAS's root README.md). JSON allows no comments, so this notice and the descriptions are fields.",
 "about": "Where each Sevopedia category's page has its panels and EXPAND buttons, at 1920x1080 windowed in a 1926x1120 window, written by map_sevopedia.py: it clicks each category point from civ4_points.json, which opens the category's first entry, and finds panels by colour and EXPAND buttons by matching civ4_expand_button.png. Boxes are [left, top, right, bottom] and buttons [x, y], window-relative. Panels are ordered top to bottom, then left to right. A panel mostly covered by pictures can be missed, as Upgrades To was on the unit page. Like the click points, these change with the resolution or the Sevopedia's code; rerun the script after such a change.",
 "page_kinds": {
  "entry pages": "Terrains to Techs except the trees and the unit chart: an entry list on the left, then panels; clicking a category opens its first entry.",
  "text pages": "Mods Info, Outdated, Hints and Shortcuts: one large text panel.",
  "media pages": "Movies and Music: an entry list, a title panel and an orange play button at the top right.",
  "table pages": "Eras, Handicaps, Speeds and World Sizes: one table filling the page, drawn darker than panels, so no panel is found; a small extra button sits left of EXIT, not identified.",
  "diagrams": "Unit Tree and Promotion Tree: a full-page diagram; Unit Chart: one table.",
  "index": "Index: every entry in three columns under a 0 1 A..Z jump bar."
 },
 "expand": {
  "text": "An EXPAND above a text panel, such as Background at (1840, 742) on a unit page, opens that text over the whole page, covering the entry list too. Its top right has TEXT, BG and STYLE settings, each with - and + buttons at about (1752, y) and (1787, y) for y 56, 87 and 117, cycling options such as 1 of 129 text sizes, and CLOSE at about (1848, 117), which returns to the page.",
  "model": "The EXPAND above a 3D view, at (1840, 97) on a unit page, shows the model over the whole page, with RELOAD at about (1755, 118) and CLOSE at about (1848, 118).",
  "tested": "2026-11-11, on the Ancient Maceman's unit page."
 },
